\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Notes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 EcoWitt data depth vs. Open-Meteo:
\f1\b0  The current conditions panel (temp, feels, rain, wind, UV, pressure) all come from your physical station via EcoWitt. The Hi/Lo and 7-day forecast come from Open-Meteo since EcoWitt only provides real-time readings, not predictions.\

\f0\b Polling interval:
\f1\b0  TRMNL refreshes on your device's configured schedule (default ~15 min). EcoWitt updates every minute from the station; Open-Meteo forecasts update hourly, so both are always fresh.\

\f0\b Pressure decimals:
\f1\b0  The template shows the integer part in the big stat and the decimal as a sub-label. If EcoWitt returns e.g. 
\f5\fs26 "1013.2"
\f1\fs24 , it renders as 
\f5\fs26 1013
\f1\fs24  + 
\f5\fs26 .2
\f1\fs24 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b\fs26 \cf0 date
\f0\fs24  filter on forecast days:
\f1\b0  The 
\f5\fs26 | date: "%a"
\f1\fs24  filter on Open-Meteo's 
\f5\fs26 "2026-04-13"
\f1\fs24  strings should work in TRMNL's Liquid. If day names show as blank, replace with a static array workaround (just hardcode Mon/Tue/Wed/Thu/Fri/Sat/Sun in order using forloop.index0).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Force Refresh:
\f1\b0  After saving, click 
\f0\b Force Refresh
\f1\b0  on the plugin settings page to pull data and check the preview before it appears on device.\
}